  "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Here's a summary of the payment terms implementation:\n\n## Summary\n\n**src/invoices.js** - Added payment terms support:\n\n1. **Helper function `lastDayOfMonth(date)`** - Calculates the last day of the month for EOM terms\n2. **Helper function `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)`** - Maps each term type to its due date:\n   - `'NET14'`: 14 days after issue date\n   - `'NET30'`: 30 days after issue date  \n   - `'EOM'`: Last day of the issue date's month\n\n3. **Updated `createInvoice()` function**:\n   - Accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to `'NET30'`)\n   - Validates terms against allowed values\n   - Returns `TERMS_INVALID` error for unknown terms\n   - Adds `terms` and `dueDate` properties to the returned invoice\n   - Terms and dueDate are preserved through subsequent operations like `issueInvoice()` and `recordPayment()`\n\n**src/errors.js** - Added error code:\n   - `TERMS_INVALID`: \"Payment terms must be \"NET14\", \"NET30\", or \"EOM\".\"\n\n**test/invoices.test.js** - Added 13 tests covering:\n   - Default NET30 terms\n   - NET14 and EOM calculation\n   - Invalid term rejection\n   - Edge cases (month boundaries, leap years, end-of-month dates)\n   - Terms preservation through operations\n   - Terms independence from discounts and line items\n\n**test/payments.test.js** - Added 1 test verifying:\n   - Payment terms and due dates are preserved when recording payments\n\n**Result:** All 182 tests pass (169 original + 13 payment terms tests)",
